  "functional_goals_and_modes": [
    "J2 5V/GND powers the USB half, MCP1700 gives 3.3V, and USB_M/P retain D-/D+ polarity to SAMD. SWD exposes CLK, DIO, 3.3V reference and a defined ground through the selected zero-ohm R4 link.",
    "J3/J4 contacts1/3/4/5 mate return/5V/TX/RX. Intact and rejoined assemblies have equivalent roles. A separated UPDI half uses one external J4.3 5V supply; never connect independent supplies together. CTS/RTS are unused.",
    "Nominal UART 9600 baud8N1 provides one-byte echo under an explicitly selected firmware model. UPDI TX LOW drives through nominal1.2kohm to J5.3, TX HIGH releases to HiZ; nominal4.7kohm pullup goes to5V and target is open-drain. Use an open-drain/level-translated host transmitter, not push-pull3.3V HIGH on this node.",
    "All released UPDI is HIGH>=0.7*5V, host or target asserted is LOW<=0.3*5V. Host releases during target response. A 5V-tolerant receiver/translator protects actual3.3V SAMD RX; no bare5V tolerance claim. Exercise intact, separated, rejoined, UART idle/data and both UPDI directions. Full flashing/USB stack and physical break forces are outside scope."
  ],
  "declared_nominal_loads": "5V source>=100mA, USB half20mA and target<=10mA; UPDI1.2kohm/4.7kohm/100pF; 5V-tolerant translation.",
  "bench_conventions": "Common return; no independent peripheral power unless a separated mode explicitly selects it. Power-off signal drivers HiZ; fixtures initialize with rails off and wait for supplies/declared component models to settle before observing states. Unused external contacts individually1Mohm to return in bench fixtures; no floating voltage is inferred. A source NC observation cannot override an explicitly selected public role.",
  "logical_model_boundary": "Declared virtual LCD/MCU/card/DRAM/module behavior is a curator-selected nominal test model. It is not installed firmware, a manufacturer guarantee, or evidence of actual source-CAD function. Detailed task fixtures and affected numerical thresholds are fixed in a later immutable task supplement before validation/admission.",
  "R1": "Schematic-only public electrical/function scope. Later reference must have actual KiCad10.0.6 all-severity zero error/zero warning, ignored[], no reduced rules/new waivers, and scoped functional positive. No implicit PCB, manufacturing, physical fit or complete external system protocol.",
